#. (itstool) path: page/title
#: C/supported-protocols.page:26
msgid "What is the technology used by Boxes?"
msgstr "Hvilken teknologi bruker Boxes?"

#. (itstool) path: page/p
#: C/supported-protocols.page:36
msgid ""
"Boxes uses <app>qemu-kvm</app>, <app>libvirt-glib</app> and <app>spice-"
"gtk</app> to allow users to easily manage virtual machines."
msgstr ""
"Boxes bruker <app>qemu-kvm</app>, <app>libvirt-glib</app> og <app>spice-"
"gtk</app> for å gi brukerne en enkel måte å administrere virtuelle maskiner."

#. (itstool) path: section/title
#: C/supported-protocols.page:41
msgid "QEMU with KVM"
msgstr "QEMU med KVM"

#. (itstool) path: section/p
#: C/supported-protocols.page:43
msgid ""
"<app>QEMU</app> is a machine emulator and virtualizer. As a machine "
"emulator, it can run OSes and programs made for one machine (e.g. an ARM "
"board) on a different machine (e.g. your own PC). As a virtualizer, QEMU "
"achieves near native performance by executing the guest code directly on the"
" host CPU using KVM."
msgstr ""
"<app>QEMU</app> er en maskinemulator og virtualiserer. Som maskinemulator "
"kan den kjøre operativsystemer og programmer laget for én maskin (f.eks. et "
"ARM-kort) på en annen maskin (f.eks. din egen PC). Som virtualiserer oppnår "
"QEMU nær native ytelse ved å kjøre gjestekoden direkte på verts-CPU-en ved "
"hjelp av KVM."

#. (itstool) path: section/p
#: C/supported-protocols.page:49
msgid ""
"<app>KVM</app> (Kernel-based Virtual Machine) is a Linux kernel module that "
"allows a user space program to use the hardware virtualization features of "
"various processors."
msgstr ""
"<app>KVM</app> (Kernel-based Virtual Machine) er et Linux-kjerne­modul som "
"lar et program i brukerrommet bruke maskinvare­virtualiserings­funksjonene "
"til ulike prosessorer."

#. (itstool) path: section/title
#: C/supported-protocols.page:56
msgid "libvirt"
msgstr "libvirt"

#. (itstool) path: section/p
#: C/supported-protocols.page:58
msgid ""
"<app>libvirt</app> is a toolkit for manipulating (creating, deleting and "
"modifying) and monitoring virtual machines."
msgstr ""
"<app>libvirt</app> er et verktøysett for å manipulere (opprette, slette og "
"endre) og overvåke virtuelle maskiner."

#. (itstool) path: section/p
#: C/supported-protocols.page:61
msgid ""
"<app>libvirt-glib</app> wraps libvirt to provide a high-level object-"
"oriented API suited for glib-based applications."
msgstr ""
"<app>libvirt-glib</app> omslutter libvirt og gir et høynivå objektorientert "
"API som passer godt for glib-baserte applikasjoner."

#. (itstool) path: section/title
#: C/supported-protocols.page:67
msgid "SPICE"
msgstr "SPICE"

#. (itstool) path: section/p
#: C/supported-protocols.page:69
msgid ""
"<app>SPICE</app>, the Simple Protocol for Independent Computing "
"Environments, is a system for accessing and controlling remote desktops "
"across a network."
msgstr ""
"<app>SPICE</app>, Simple Protocol for Independent Computing Environments, er"
" et system for å få tilgang til og styre fjernskrivebord over et nettverk."

#. (itstool) path: section/p
#: C/supported-protocols.page:73
msgid ""
"The SPICE server is a library that runs inside the QEMU binary. It is mainly"
" responsible for authentication of client connections, relaying of graphics "
"output of the guest OS to the client and relaying of user input (mouse and "
"keyboard) from client to guest."
msgstr ""
"SPICE-serveren er et bibliotek som kjører inne i QEMU-binæren. Den har "
"hovedansvaret for å autentisere klienttilkoblinger, sende grafisk utdata fra"
" gjest-OS-en til klienten og sende brukerinput (mus og tastatur) fra klient "
"til gjest."

#. (itstool) path: section/p
#: C/supported-protocols.page:78
msgid ""
"<app>spice-gtk</app> is the SPICE client that provides a view into the guest"
" OS."
msgstr ""
"<app>spice-gtk</app> er SPICE-klienten som gir et vindu inn i gjest-OS-en."

